                <pb facs="0402" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/3559: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-23T12:00:00-05:00">June 23,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>94. My 91, June 22, 4 p.m. I am informed that within the next few days certain of
                    the opposition factions will publish in the United States declarations of the
                    reasons which have caused them to accept my tender of good offices. Probably a
                    good many of these declarations which will be intended to appeal to the most
                    radical of the members of the opposition, will either misconstrue or exaggerate
                    the essential character of my services. It will be helpful if the Department <pb
                        facs="0403" n="315" xml:id="pg315"/> would refuse to issue any opinion
                    regarding such declarations and merely limit itself to stating that the official
                    interpretation given by the Cuban Government to my tender of good offices is
                    clearly defined in the editorial in the Government organ <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Heraldo de Cuba of</hi> June 22 of which portions were quoted in my
                    telegram under reference and full copy and translation of which are being sent
                    to the Department today by air mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
